# Website quality

Use this when changing public pages, navigation, footer content, the document shell, or the production web build.

- The logo returns home. Phone numbers use `tel:` and email addresses use `mailto:` when those contacts exist.
- Internal links resolve. A custom 404 exists for unknown public routes. The visible copyright year is the current year.
- Favicon, title, and meta description are present on public pages. The current document title is `Velora`.
- Empty, loading, success, and error feedback exist on user-facing flows.
- The production build does not ship a dev overlay, framework watermark, or public source map.
- Images declare dimensions or a stable placeholder and include alt text.
- There is no placeholder copy on a page that is presented as finished.

The full audit list is in `docs/quality/website-quality.md`. Run the `website-quality-audit` skill before calling a public page done.
